Description: Don't issue TLSv1.3 session tickets on FTPS data connections
 Since 1.3.9e (Issue #2367) mod_tls declines to encrypt new session tickets
 for data transfers. OpenSSL 1.1.1 and older 3.x (jammy's 3.0.2) then still
 send an empty NewSessionTicket, malformed for TLSv1.3, and clients abort
 every data transfer (curl: "length mismatch", GnuTLS: "Error in parsing").
Origin: other, https://github.com/proftpd/proftpd/pull/2417
Bug: https://github.com/proftpd/proftpd/issues/2416
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-28
---
--- a/contrib/mod_tls.c
+++ b/contrib/mod_tls.c
@@ -7723,6 +7723,20 @@
       }
     }
 #endif /* PR_USE_OPENSSL_SSL_SESSION_TICKET_CALLBACK */
+
+#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x10101000L && \
+    defined(TLS1_3_VERSION)
+    /* Do not issue any new TLSv1.3 session tickets on data connections
+     * (Issue #2367).  Declining in tls_ticket_key_cb() is not sufficient:
+     * OpenSSL versions before 3.0 then send a malformed, empty TLSv1.3
+     * NewSessionTicket message, which clients reject (Issue #2416).
+     */
+    if (SSL_set_num_tickets(ssl, 0) != 1) {
+      pr_trace_msg(trace_channel, 3,
+        "error disabling TLSv1.3 session tickets for data transfer: %s",
+        tls_get_errors());
+    }
+#endif /* OpenSSL 1.1.1 or later */
   }
 
   retry:
